From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: sun8i-ce - Take the resets as an array

The crypto engine of the A733 has two resets, one for the engine and
one for its CE_SYS part (A733 manual, 4.1.6.118). The driver asks for
one reset without a name and gets only the first.

Take all resets of the node as one array. With the single reset of the
earlier SoCs the array holds that reset, and asserting and deasserting
it works as before.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: both resets of the A733 engine are released
on probe and the engine runs.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun8i-ce/sun8i-ce-core.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun8i-ce/sun8i-ce-core.c b/drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun8i-ce/sun8i-ce-core.c
index 21762bd408e5..7ae28e692295 100644
--- a/drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun8i-ce/sun8i-ce-core.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/allwinner/sun8i-ce/sun8i-ce-core.c
@@ -958,7 +958,7 @@ static int sun8i_ce_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (irq < 0)
 		return irq;
 
-	ce->reset = devm_reset_control_get(&pdev->dev, NULL);
+	ce->reset = devm_reset_control_array_get_exclusive(&pdev->dev);
 	if (IS_ERR(ce->reset))
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, PTR_ERR(ce->reset),
 				     "No reset control found\n");
